{"actor":"agent:qa-adversarial","data":{"description":"AUDIT ITEMS 1/6/7. REPRO: in a repo, run the hook sequence from a nested subdir (src/deep/nested). RESULT: .etch/ is created at src/deep/nested/.etch, NOT at the repo root.\nIMPACT: (1) .etch/settings.json at the repo root is SILENTLY IGNORED for any session not started at the exact repo root -> custom redaction_patterns, raw_machine_identity, recovery_timeout_hours all stop applying (security-relevant: redaction silently weakens). (2) crash .wip files scatter into per-subdir .etch dirs; the recovery sweep (which scans <cwd>/.etch/sessions) won't find orphans created under a different cwd. (3) buffer fragmentation across the tree.\nROOT CAUSE: hooks/common.go findRepoRoot() returns os.Getwd() and never walks up. FIX: use 'git rev-parse --show-toplevel'. Verified empirically in /tmp/etch-subdir.","priority":"medium","short_id":"ETCH-34","status":"backlog","title":".etch dir + settings.json resolved from CWD not git root; subdir sessions ignore config","type":"bug"},"id":"ev_01KSTXS9TZ0NED0RR1Z7CCHQR2","schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KSTXS9TY054Y1S6GSPNDQ1TV","ts":"2026-05-29T22:30:55Z","type":"task_created"}
{"actor":{"agent_type":"review","base_name":"Etch-Reviewer","framework":"claude-code","model":"claude-opus-4-8","name":"Etch-Reviewer-1","serial":1,"session":"sess_01KTAH0J43J0KC6GCCMT3DVB8A"},"data":{"field":"priority","from":"medium","to":"high"},"id":"ev_01KTAH230WG9FF7TAPA04EPEGE","schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KSTXS9TY054Y1S6GSPNDQ1TV","ts":"2026-06-04T23:56:22Z","type":"field_updated"}
{"actor":{"agent_type":"review","base_name":"Etch-Reviewer","framework":"claude-code","model":"claude-opus-4-8","name":"Etch-Reviewer-1","serial":1,"session":"sess_01KTAH0J43J0KC6GCCMT3DVB8A"},"data":{"body":"Severity upgraded medium\u2192high by the 2026-06-04 deep review (ETCH-40 finding #2). The CWD anchoring is worse than a config miss: findRepoRoot()=os.Getwd() anchors the .etch/sessions wip + ULID mapping to each hook process's CWD, so when hooks for one session fire from different CWDs (subdir, linked worktree), session_end's LookupMapping returns '' and takes the silent printOK() path \u2014 the session is DROPPED with no record, and recovery never scans the other CWD's .etch so the orphan is unrecoverable. Fix at the boundary: resolve git common-dir root once (gitstate.go already does this correctly for the recorded field) and thread it everywhere. Coordinate with ETCH-40 \u2014 fixing #2 there closes this too."},"id":"ev_01KTAH2341GCQVRJQXKKRP1Z7P","schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KSTXS9TY054Y1S6GSPNDQ1TV","ts":"2026-06-04T23:56:23Z","type":"comment_added"}
